Use <cstdint> instead of glibc's internal <bits/stdint-uintn.h> in the Level
Zero backend.

<bits/stdint-uintn.h> is a glibc implementation detail that merely typedefs
uintN_t; it does not exist outside glibc, so the Level Zero backend fails to
compile on Windows with:

    src/runtime/ze/ze_code_object.cpp(19,10):
        fatal error: 'bits/stdint-uintn.h' file not found

Including it is incorrect even on Linux (programs should never include
bits/*.h directly); it just happens to work there. <cstdint> is the portable
spelling and provides exactly the same typedefs.

diff --git a/src/runtime/ze/ze_code_object.cpp b/src/runtime/ze/ze_code_object.cpp
--- a/src/runtime/ze/ze_code_object.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/ze/ze_code_object.cpp
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 #include "hipSYCL/runtime/ze/ze_queue.hpp"
 #include "hipSYCL/runtime/error.hpp"
 #include <algorithm>
-#include <bits/stdint-uintn.h>
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <level_zero/ze_api.h>
 #include <cassert>
 #include <string>
